// The Lance -- four sounds, namespaced so this drops into any mod without
// colliding with its sound names.
//
// lnc/loop is the one that matters: it is started with CHANF_LOOPING on
// CHAN_5 when the trigger goes down and pitched every tic after, so the
// approaching cook-off is audible before it is visible. CHAN_5 rather than
// a lower channel so it does not fight a mod's own weapon or item sounds.

lnc/charge    PLCHRG
lnc/loop      PLALTF
lnc/cookoff   PLCOUT
lnc/empty     AKEMPT
lnc/sizzle    AKEMPT

// ---- burning deaths -------------------------------------------------
//
// TWO $random GROUPS, THREE TAKES EACH, and the pyre rolls which group as
// well as letting the engine roll within it -- so six distinct screams,
// picked twice over, plus a per-play pitch shift of +/-12%. A room of
// burning zombies is a chorus instead of one sound played six times.
$random lnc/burn/scream1 { lnc/burn/zob1 lnc/burn/zob2 lnc/burn/zob3 }
$random lnc/burn/scream2 { lnc/burn/zom1 lnc/burn/zom2 lnc/burn/zom3 }

lnc/burn/zob1   BURNZOB1
lnc/burn/zob2   BURNZOB2
lnc/burn/zob3   BURNZOB3
lnc/burn/zom1   BURNZOM1
lnc/burn/zom2   BURNZOM2
lnc/burn/zom3   BURNZOM3

// The crackle under it all, looped on CHAN_BODY for the pyre's lifetime
// and stopped explicitly when it burns out.
lnc/burn/loop   DSFLAME
